A||||5||firstfiero||How they score cars at shows?||||14||
Z||000000||firstfiero||08-11-2001||11:21 AM||||      This weekend at the holiday inn the z club is in town. I was talking to a guy with a sweet 280z and asked him if he drove it their? He laughed and said of course if you don't they knock points off in the competition. 10 pts are automaticaly deducted if you have a trailor queen. Are any of the fiero shows like that? I mean it's more impressive to me to have a spotless car in a show when you drove 8 hrs to get their.<BR>     I'm going to take some pics tomorrow...their was a guy there with 10 grand into his paint job alone. anybody else like z cars?<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||AusFiero||08-11-2001||12:27 PM||||Well I just wish they new how to judge Fieros at all in Australia. Only had 1 Fiero class in our Pontiac Nationals and it was for best original Fiero. Well there was 4 cars, I got second, narrowly. But what p1ssed me off was I got marked down severely for redoing my interior in custon colours and putting a sub in. The only mods from original and it looks almost indy like anyway. <BR>    The car that won had a Holden engine in it, a Holden dashboard, SAAS seats that didnt even match the interior.<BR>    Well I questioned the so called judges the next morning after the presentation and asked how the hell could a Holden in a Fiero body win the best original Fiero over mine. Response, oh we seen your flash interior and thought the other must hve been original because it was grey and stuff. Judges didn't even know what a Fiero was supposed to have in it. Like I thought the 3800 that was upside down on the Holden engines Plenium cover shoulda given it away personally, oh and the Holden written on the gauges. Then to top it off his Holden engined Fiero won best "original" engine bay. The guy shoulda knocked back both trophies as he knew his car was neither original for either category and the judges had no clue. He robbed me of a trophy and he robbed many an outstanding original engine bay of their just deserves.<P>Some judges should not be judges.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||08-11-2001||12:28 PM||||All shows have different criteria for judging.<P>Some cars get trailered to the shows because four people want to come and have one Fiero to show.<P>Some have very low milage cars which they want to keep that way.<P>The show sponsors classify cars differently.  Some shows have 'professioanl judges'. There are shows with peer judging and shows with mixed judging.<P>If you own a Fiero and go to shows to win a trophy only, you are on the wrong show car tour.  Fiero shows IMHO are for driving the car to the show and seeing other cars.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||08-11-2001||12:49 PM||||First of all, let me say that I love the Z cars- well OK thr 240-280, not quite so fond of the 300 - but its only because I LOVE the body style.  Next car I fix up will be a Datsun.  There was a guy who worked at the host hotel at Natls who had an in progress 240 and he was a real nice guy, interested in Fieros too.<P>As far as judging, well how can any judge tell that you trailed in, really?  The only signifigance in trailering I've seen is a couple shows with Trailered car classes.<P>I trailered to Daytona in 2000 cause 3 people went to the show and the Fiero kinda only fits 2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||08-11-2001||02:40 PM||||The shows I go to are judged by the people. I vote for the car that is <P>#1 driven to the show.<BR>#2 Very Clean.<BR>#3 Has the Deck and Hood open(Unless it is high mileage class.<BR>#4 you can tell the owner takes pride in the car.<BR>#5 has that special something, I can tell which one when I see it. The car will grab my attention. <P><BR>How I don't judge. <BR>#1 I don't care about the amount of money put into the car, color, or what engine it has in it. I vote on the way the car looks and how clean it is. <BR>#2 I personally don't like it when cars have a blanket or rug under and around it. I think it is a way to keep people away from the car so you can't see the cars faults. Just my opinion. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by 88CoupeV6 (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000005||Jaygee79||08-11-2001||03:09 PM||||I pretty much agree with what Josh said, but I also consider (if possible) how much work the owner themself has done or had done.  I just don't see it as much of an accomplishment if you buy a car in perfect condition and don't have to do anything to it.  I know a lot of people don't agree with me, and that's fine.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR>ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggypic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
